<title>USA: Pinnacle Brands postpones IPO.</title>
<headline>Pinnacle Brands postpones IPO.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pinnacle Brands Inc has postponed its planned initial public offering due to market conditions, according to lead underwriter Merrill Lynch.</p>
<p>The company, which sells hockey, baseball and football trading cards, had planned a $60 million IPO in September.</p>
<p>The company has posted net losses since 1993, according to its prospectus. Its baseball and hockey card sales have not yet recovered from a slump suffered after the 1994 Major League Baseball strike and work stoppage at the National Hockey League.  Pinnacle posted a 1995 net loss of $2.4 million on revenues of $130.2 million.</p>
</text>
